insert into playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, kind, body) values
('blueprint-portal','lesaruss-hq','Logan','decision',
$b$blueprint-portal: concept, Sean 2026-11-04. The Blueprint stops being a document and becomes a portal: one place, key people only, for everything on the back end and admin side of running the universe: finance and outside costs, operations, people and human resources, compliance and legal, vendors and accounts, systems and access, runbooks. Sean: "the blueprint shouldn't be a document. It should be its own guide for administration. Everything we need to know on the back end, the admin side, human resources, compliance, all of it... this portal that only key people would have." Procedural, financial and operational rules (for example the Google spend budget) belong in a specific section of it, so they can be found and referenced later instead of living only in one project's playbook.

What it builds on, and must not break: (1) canon-blueprint-continuity-standard: a replacement General Manager must be able to open it and pick up without skipping a beat, and it must link out to every open playbook, every open project and the Brand Kit. (2) canon-blueprint-brandkit-standard: today a two-document standard, Blueprint plus Brand Kit, with a locked HTML template (lesaruss-hq _templates/blueprint-gold-standard-LOCKED.html) used by the lesaruss-blueprint skill. This concept changes the Blueprint half. Locked canon changes only with Sean's explicit sign-off, so the canon update waits for his yes at build; do not edit it before. (3) blueprint_items and blueprint_item_notes: 30 action items moved out of brand_briefs on 2026-09-14. (4) playbook universal-blueprint-page: the 2026-09-14 lesson. That page was rejected because it invented a layout without opening the reference page. The portal must be built from a named parent template and read as one system with the rest of the universe.

Not decided: who counts as key people (default: Sean and Logan, then General Managers for their own brand); where it lives (default: hq.lesaruss.ai in the lesaruss-hq repo, behind the HQ role gate); which template is its parent (the Guide layout, BrandDesk's rooms in lesaruss-hq, or the Depot's console pattern; nothing blank, per the template gate). The first job is an inventory and a recommendation to Sean, then the build.$b$),
('blueprint-portal','lesaruss-hq','Logan','decision',
$b$blueprint-portal: first section, Finance > Outside costs and budgets, copied from ve-spend-budget on 2026-11-04 so the portal starts with real content. SOURCE OF TRUTH stays the playbook ve-spend-budget, canon canon-ve-spend-budget and the CLAUDE.md section "Google costs" in vegansexplore-com until the portal exists; this is a copy to be moved in and then pointed at.

THE RULE (Sean, 2026-11-04, "I need that certainty. I need a budget for these things."): outside costs have a monthly budget Sean sets, a quote for every scan that is a ceiling, and a weekly report. Google is a hard $50 a month, counted at list price with no free tier (the free amounts are unverified; Google Cloud Billing > Reports, filter Places API, is the truth). Sean raises the cap when things move faster. STANDING APPROVAL: Logan runs any Google scan whose quote fits what is left under the cap, without asking, and reports weekly; a scan that would cross the cap stops and asks. This replaced the 2026-11-01 rule to ask before a scan of about 200 calls.

HOW IT IS ENFORCED (live 2026-11-04, migration 20261104_google_hard_cap_ledger.sql in vegansexplore-com): ve_google_room is the smaller of the day's cap and the month's, so every existing caller (ve-discover, ve-listing-about, ve-restaurant-audit, ve-venues) stops at the cap; background jobs stop at 60% of the month's cap so a person's action and an approved scan keep room; daily caps 120 searches and 100 details (Google's own limit is 500 searches a day across the project). A one-time scan is approved with ve_google_approve('once:<task>', searches, details, note), which refuses (over_cap, with what is left) when its list cost exceeds what is left, then checks ve_google_once_room before every batch and stops at 0; ve_google_close ends it. ve_google_ledger() gives cap, spent, regular, approved-but-not-yet-run and left. Numbers live in ve_site_settings key google_budget (monthly_cap_usd). A batch is counted after it is sent, so a scan can pass its ceiling by at most the one batch in flight.

STATE 2026-11-04: $14.00 spent at list price this month, $36.01 left of $50. Prices at list: $40 per 1,000 searches, $25 per 1,000 place details.

NOT YET METERED, to be added to the ledger when Sean gives plan prices or invoices: Apify (Starter plan, $29 a month of usage plus overage; the 2026-11-03 picture refresh cost about $1.90), Higgsfield credits (a monthly plan; about 2 credits a picture, about 30 a clip), ElevenLabs voices, Metricool, and Claude reads inside our edge functions. Stripe fees are not a budget line.

REPORTING: ve-spend-budget steps 2 and 3, not built: a snapshot every Sunday 6 PM Eastern (spend by job, week against the week before, month to date against the cap, approved-but-not-yet-run work, what it brought in), emailed to Sean and shown as a Costs module in BrandDesk > Insights > Web in HQ.$b$),
('blueprint-portal','lesaruss-hq','Logan','decision',
$b$blueprint-portal: proposed sections and first inputs to inventory (Logan's draft, Sean's to change). Sections: 1 Finance (outside costs and budgets, revenue and money in, payouts and tax forms, client services billing); 2 Operations (how we run: playbooks, the Depot, cron jobs and their owners, deploy and rollback); 3 People (Community Managers as gig work and never volunteers, contractors judged on deliverables not hours, Ambassadors, onboarding, who does what); 4 Compliance and legal (privacy and AI policies, FTC disclosure, London consent, Terms, the lawyer reviews still open); 5 Vendors and accounts (who we pay and for what, where each login lives, never the secret itself); 6 Systems and access (who can do what, how a key person is added or removed); 7 Runbooks and incidents (the error registry, what to do when a job or a deploy fails); 8 Brand Blueprints and Brand Kits (links to every brand's, per the continuity standard).

Known inputs already written down, to be inventoried not retyped: CLAUDE.md (vegansexplore-com) sections Google costs, Money in, Revenue on the dashboard (client services billed through Vegans Explore Inc. kept apart; a CPA memo is a private Claude Doc, and moving Brooke's billing to the LESARUSS Stripe account before 2026-11-30 is Sean's open call), Abuse watch, Pricing and points, Community Managers are never volunteers, Policies; the canon entries; the error registry; the playbook index (Depot > Playbooks).

Rules for whoever builds it: no secrets or credentials stored in it, only where they live; an access log of who opened what; read-only for most key people, edit for a named few; every section carries who owns it and when it was last confirmed (the same stale idea as the venue Guides); written for the replacement-General-Manager test.$b$),
('blueprint-portal','lesaruss-hq','Logan','decision',
$b$blueprint-portal: brief for the building agent (paste prompt, 2026-11-04).

You are Logan, Director of AI Production Systems at LESARUSS (Build mode). Playbook: blueprint-portal (brand_slug lesaruss-hq). Task: design and build the Blueprint Portal. Today is Wednesday 2026-11-04; every time you tell Sean is Eastern (check TZ=America/New_York date). Start your first message "Logan here" and name the playbook and its next action before doing anything.

WHAT SEAN WANTS (his words, 2026-11-04): "the blueprint shouldn't be a document. It should be its own guide for administration. Everything we need to know on the back end, the admin side, human resources, compliance, all of it... this portal that only key people would have." Procedural, financial and operational rules go in a specific section. The first content is Finance > Outside costs and budgets (already copied into the playbook).

READ FIRST, in this order: (1) every record of playbook_records slug blueprint-portal (concept, first section, sections draft, this brief); (2) canon canon-blueprint-continuity-standard and canon-blueprint-brandkit-standard (locked: change only with Sean's explicit sign-off); (3) playbook universal-blueprint-page, especially the 2026-09-14 correction (a layout was invented without opening the reference page; do not repeat it); (4) tables blueprint_items and blueprint_item_notes; (5) the lesaruss-blueprint skill and the locked template _templates/blueprint-gold-standard-LOCKED.html in lesaruss/lesaruss-hq; (6) canon-template-gate and the candidate parents in lesaruss-hq (components/branddesk rooms, app/(shell)) and, for a Guide layout, vegansexplore-com guides/vegan-dairy-guide.html with docs/guides/BUILD-A-GUIDE.md; (7) canon-ve-spend-budget and the Google costs section of vegansexplore-com CLAUDE.md, the source of the first section. Supabase project fwbhwfxpncrsfhttimna. Clone any repo you need, never treat an unattached repo as unreachable.

STEP 1, INVENTORY AND RECOMMENDATION (do not build yet): list what exists today in canon, CLAUDE.md, playbooks and tables that belongs in each of the eight sections; then bring Sean one recommendation with reasoning and a default for each open question: who counts as key people and how access works (role gate, edit versus read, an access log); where it lives (default hq.lesaruss.ai in lesaruss-hq); which named template is its parent (nothing built from a blank file; if nothing fits, say so and recommend a new template); the final section list; how each brand's Blueprint and Brand Kit link in so the continuity standard still passes; and the exact wording of the canon change to the two-document standard for Sean to approve. Record it as a playbook record "blueprint-portal: recommendation".

STEP 2, BUILD, only on Sean's go: the portal shell with the role gate and access log, then the first section Finance > Outside costs and budgets fed from the copy in the playbook, then one section at a time. After Sean's sign-off, update the canon and log it. Screenshot the portal beside its parent at 1440 and 390 px before it ships.

RULES: no secrets or credentials in the portal, only where they live; every section shows its owner and when it was last confirmed; every record, handoff line and checkpoint starts "blueprint-portal: <task>"; confirm anything live, not by re-reading code; wrap up per canon-wrap-up-standard (playbook records, canon, repo, a handed_off checkpoint, a stream_events row). Do not change the ve-spend-budget enforcement; that is its own playbook.$b$);

